<BaseLayout locale="en" title="About Rutas B" description="Meet the guide and discover the perspective behind Rutas B de Barcelona."><header class="page-hero"><div><p class="kicker">About Rutas B</p><h1>A guide to help you see,<br />not a list to memorise.</h1><p>Rutas B grows from a particular understanding of cultural mediation: clarity, context and conversation in front of the real city.</p></div></header><section class="section guide-panel"><figure class="guide-photo"><img src={base+'images/guia/daniel-pinto.png'} alt="Daniel Pinto, guide at Rutas B de Barcelona" /></figure><div><p class="kicker dark">Your guide</p><h2>Daniel Pinto</h2><p class="large-copy">Tour guide in training and sociologist, focused on turning complex phenomena into clear, approachable and useful stories for people visiting Barcelona.</p><p>For questions about tours, private groups or collaborations, please use the contact page.</p><a class="button outline" href={root+'contacto/'}>Contact</a></div></section><section class="section editorial-layout"><div><p class="kicker dark">The project</p><h2>Barcelona as an experience that can be learned</h2></div><div><p class="large-copy">Each tour begins with a question and organises the way we look around it. The aim is not to accumulate names and dates, but to recognise relationships between architecture and city, heritage and everyday life, history and the present.</p><p>The tours are prepared through research, fieldwork, practical testing and adaptation to the audience. Commercial information that is not yet final is clearly marked as pending.</p></div></section></BaseLayout>
